Arel woke and struck the seed with her beak. The crack widened into the first horizon, and the green stone slipped out, unfolding into earth. Her footsteps pressed valleys into it; her lifted wings raised hills. When she shook sleep from her feathers, the drops became springs, and the springs hurried together as rivers.

